        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "57e9ba7c-eb80-5cca-89b5-b71f754575bf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John O'Hara, Bobbie Ann Mason, Gene Stone, Alan Furst, Michael Kinsley, Joel Kotkin\n- Works: Elizabeth Appleton\n- Organizations: Esquire Magazine\n- Roles: writer, novelist, short story writer, essayist, literary critic, senior editor\n- Topics: social status, manners, social realism\n\nFacts:\n- John O'Hara was born on January 31, 1905, and he became an American writer known for observing social status and manners in early to mid-20th-century America.\n- John O'Hara was regarded as pre-eminent among his contemporaries in depicting social realism.\n- Bobbie Ann Mason was born on May 1, 1940, and she is a Southern United States novelist, short story writer, essayist, and literary critic from Kentucky.\n- John O'Hara published the novel Elizabeth Appleton in 1963.\n- John O'Hara died on April 11, 1970.\n- Gene Stone later worked as a senior editor at Esquire Magazine.\n- At Esquire Magazine, Gene Stone edited authors including Alan Furst, Bobbie Ann Mason, Michael Kinsley, and Joel Kotkin.",
